/// Deploys the app to a platform made with esquadro (esquadro new -starter
/// platform), from its CI: each tag v* publishes the image, then signs in
/// to the server with a key that can only deploy this app, and deploys the
/// tag. The server pulls the image, migrates the database, replaces the
/// containers and, when they are not healthy, goes back to the version
/// before; the CI fails with the reason. The repository needs three
/// secrets, which the platform's task app:key gives it: DEPLOY_SSH_KEY,
/// DEPLOY_HOST and DEPLOY_KNOWN_HOSTS. Behind the platform's Caddy, the app
/// trusts the visitor's address it passes.
blueprint deploy {
  version "0.1.0"
  requires docker, github_actions
  optional http
}
